      "description": "Watch HEBC Hamburg vs Borussia Dortmund highlights and goals from DFB-Pokal on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 1, 2026. The stage was set for a highly anticipated DFB Pokal clash, with both sides looking to make their mark on this crisp matchday on September 1, 2026. Dortmund Takes Command From the opening minutes, Borussia Dortmund signaled their intent, pinning Hamburg-Eimsbütteler BC back into their own half. The breakthrough arrived in the 33rd minute when a moment of misfortune for the hosts resulted in an own goal by Janek Wrede . This incident opened the floodgates; just moments later, Daniel Svensson doubled the lead in the 36th minute with a clinical finish. As the first half drew to a close, Samuele Inácio took center stage, scoring twice in quick succession at the 41st and 45+2 minute marks, putting the match firmly beyond reach by the interval with a 4-0 lead. A Professional Conclusion Following the restart, Borussia Dortmund continued to dictate the tempo of the match. Despite the introduction of fresh legs from the bench, the visitors remained relentless in their pursuit of goals. In the 59th minute, Fábio Silva put the finishing touch on a well-worked team move, assisted by Joey Veerman , to make it 5-0. While HEBC Hamburg fought to gain a consolation goal, the defensive line of the visitors stayed firm. The match concluded with a commanding 5-0 victory for Borussia Dortmund , showcasing their superior squad depth and quality in this cup fixture."
