      "description": "Watch Wehen Wiesbaden vs Bayer Leverkusen highlights and goals from DFB-Pokal on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 22, 2026. The stage was set for a classic DFB Pokal encounter as Wehen Wiesbaden hosted the formidable Bayer Leverkusen . Anticipation was high as the home side looked to bridge the gap against their top-tier opponents in a match that promised intensity and tactical intrigue. Schick Breaks the Deadlock On August 22, 2026, the match began with Bayer Leverkusen establishing dominance through possession and high pressing. While Wehen Wiesbaden remained disciplined, occasionally threatening through Justin Janitzek , the visitors' persistent attacking play finally found a crack in the defense. Afonso ira and Malik Tillman were instrumental in pulling the home defense out of position. The breakthrough arrived in the 43rd minute. After a period of sustained pressure, Malik Tillman found Patrik Schick in the center of the box. The Czech forward calmly slotted a left-footed shot into the bottom right corner, giving the Bundesliga giants a well-deserved lead just before the halftime whistle. Leverkusen Assert Their Authority The second half began with a flourish as Bayer Leverkusen doubled their advantage in the 47th minute. Lucas Vázquez showed great predatory instincts, pouncing on a loose ball in the six-yard box to fire home. This goal effectively deflated the home side's hopes of a comeback, allowing Leverkusen to rotate their squad and maintain a high tempo. As the match progressed, the visitors' depth proved decisive. In the 69th minute, a lightning-fast break saw Ibrahim Maza release Nathan Tella , who unleashed a magnificent strike into the top right corner. The scoring was completed in the 79th minute by substitute Christian Kofane , who converted a precise pass from Afonso ira . The match concluded with a professional 4-0 victory for Leverkusen, showcasing their clinical efficiency in front of goal."
